### Firewall policy — read this as directional

The rules are **directional and stateful**. In particular:

> **The recorder opens the connection to the camera. The camera can never open a connection to
> anything.**

A rule written simply as "block the camera VLAN" is *not* equivalent — it would either break
recording or leave a return path open. If a future technician replaces this policy with a simple
block, recording stops or security is lost.

Consequences you already know about, restated here for whoever comes next:

- Cameras have **no internet access**, so a time server runs inside the camera segment. Without it,
  recordings carry the wrong timestamps and lose their evidentiary value.
- Camera firmware updates are a **manual, scheduled task**, not automatic.
- **Manufacturer camera apps will not work.** Everything is viewed through the single system
  interface. This is by design.

