## 7. Continuity — how to hand this system to another provider

This section exists because you should never be trapped with us. Everything another competent
provider needs:

1. **What is installed** — section 1 of this document, with catalogue references and circuits.
2. **How it is addressed** — section 2, with the full VLAN plan and the directional firewall policy.
   Point out to them that the camera rule is directional; it is the rule most often broken on
   handover.
3. **Where the credentials are** — section 4. The vault is yours and runs on your hardware.
4. **How it is backed up and restored** — section 5, plus the restore procedure supplied with your
   system.
5. **What software it runs** — the licence appendix delivered with your system lists every component,
   its pinned version, its licence and its upstream repository. **None of it is modified by us**, so
   there is no private fork for anyone to inherit.
6. **How the configuration is built** — your system is generated from versioned templates plus a
   variables file, not hand-built. Ask us for a copy of your variables file at any time; it is yours.

None of this requires our cooperation. That is the point.

